				<blockquote class="bb_blockquote with_author"><div class="bb_quoteauthor">Originally posted by <b><a href="#c572679490124152898">Rick Deckard</a></b>:</div><blockquote class="bb_blockquote with_author"><div class="bb_quoteauthor">Originally posted by <b><a href="#c572679173080027684">Naughty Pig</a></b>:</div>No way to find out right now. Discord got raided by another indie dev spamming slurs and regular anti-ai psychosis, so it's under quarantine now. </blockquote><br>of course you'd be someone in the server 😭😭 <br><br>So you know exactly who I am and what I have access too. <br><br>the person spamming slurs wasn't an indie dev, it was some kid you buffoon<br><br>What a chud </blockquote>Dare I join a game server to check on updates so some immature forum &quot;AI specialist&quot; can't make ad-hominem.<br><br>Yes I know who you are, a meat bag on two legs like I said in another comment.<br><br>The person spamming slurs did also promote another indie game while doing so. And in the end it doesn't if it was dev himself.<br><br>You are yet again using some moralist argument &quot;oh but no human input&quot;, who cares if in the end the product works? Prompting is human input objectively. It is a moral argument to say the dev must do something beyond that. That by side, you still didn't provide a single evidence to your claims apart from visual observation and something like &quot;but it's obvious.&quot;<br><br>Vibe coding multiplayer could pose a real issue and a threat to players if security is on a low level.<br><br>The game appeared on Steam just a few days ago. Back in the day people used a lot of store assets and replaced them with time. Today people use AI assets. No difference. Expecting a game to be full of own assets from the start is very unrealistic for early access.			</div>
			<div class="comment_footer_ctn">
									<div class="forum_audit">
			Last edited by <a href="https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561199248857771" class="hoverunderline">Naughty Pig</a>;
